1b[48;5;234m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\                                          \u001b[49m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m  Exit \u001b[48;5;234m0\u001b[49m = all rows summed; exit \u001b[48;5;234m2\u001b[49m = rows were skipped.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;252mThe distinction, not hidden:\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m 160.00 covers the \u001b[1mfour\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m valid rows only. The three invalid\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mrows (lines 6\u20138: \u001b[48;5;234mNaN\u001b[49m/\u001b[48;5;234mInfinity\u001b[49m/\u001b[48;5;234mtypo\u001b[49m, all rejected with a warning on stderr) are still\u001b[39m                                                     \u001b[38;5;252m\u276e\r\n\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;5;252munresolved, so \u001b[1m160.00 is provisional\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;252m \u2014 not the complete reimbursement. Fix lines 6\u20138\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mwith real amounts (or get finance to confirm they stay excluded) and rerun before\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mtreating the total as final.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n    \u001b[38;5;243m\u00b7 resumed \u00b7 september reimbursement report handoff process\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;243m\u00b7 \u001b[38;5;116mesc\u001b[38;5;243m interrupts \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;116mctrl+c\u001b[38;5;243m quits \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;116m?\u001b[38;5;243m for help\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;110m\u2713\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m3 tasks done\u001b[38;5;243m \u00b7 2m05s \u00b7 ctrl+o expand \u00b7 /dismiss\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;146m\u203a \u001b[38;5;110mBefore I reuse this for October, I realized a bank export can contain an entire quarter. Our CLI currently sums every date. Add a --\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;110mmonth YYYY-MM option so I can safely produce a report for one month from a mixed-month export. Keep text, JSON and CSV working, exact\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;110mcents, and the current invalid-row warnings. Use a separate mixed-month fixture to prove September stays correct and October excludes\u001b[39m\r\n 