 malformed date must not silently disappear because the month filter skips it. Report the\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;103msource line on stderr and use the same partial-report exit code 2, while continuing valid rows. Please test an impossible date as well\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;103mas a malformed --month argument.\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mswitching bad dates to skip-plus-warn (exit 2) instead of a hard error\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252madding month and bad-date tests\u001b[39m\r\n    \u001b[38;5;103m\u270e edited 1 file\u001b[39m                                                                                                     \u001b[38;5;235m\u2191\u001b[38;5;243m 59.9k\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;5;235m\u2193\u001b[38;5;243m 14.3k\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;243m\u2500 \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;116mdeepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash\u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;243m (together):auto \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;173m\u25c7 YOLO\u001b[38;5;243m \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \u001b[39m   \u001b[38;5;110m$0.17\u001b[38;5;243m \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;110m\u27f2 saved $0.0569 \u00b7 86% cached\u001b[38;5;243m   \u001b[38;5;110m59.9k/1M \u00b7 6%\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;5;146m\u2827\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;146mworking\u001b[38;5;243m \u00b7 \u001b[38;5;146m55s\u001b[38;5;243m \u2500\r\n\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;243m\u203a \u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\r\n \u001b[38;5;116mesc\u001b[38;5;243m interrupt\u001b[39m                                                              \u001b[38;5;243mproject: /tmp/codeaf-sustained-1607/final/reimbursement-project\u001b[39m"]
